  "readme": "# Episode 13: thirty reviewed original character identities\n\nSave only 30 explicit character fields after the preserved original-frame and independent resource-identity reviews. Root did not view images. The original source JPEGs selected by these changes are retained by digest; original model/CG resources and existing packaged payloads remain locked by their exact source/current hashes.\n\nThese are static identity bindings. Source-cache timestamps are nominal historical anchors, not newly measured original PTS. Body, face, extra layers, complete entry/exit, original CSV phases, audible listening, geometry, timing and whole-scene/episode/gameplay acceptance remain incomplete. Uncertain model variants and choice-UI portraits are excluded according to the source and peer decisions.\n\nNormal native_repair staging, complete undo review, native_install audit/apply and full saved-field verification were performed separately. Complete ordered native documents undo to the parent by reverting only the selected character leaves; all text, voices, branches, commands, unrelated unknown fields, other139 scene pairs and protected22 files are preserved. Review-side evidence appends and selected-field-warning removals remain draft, and only one owned batch is added. No frontend change or invented link/background/BGM/animation is included.\n\nThe user's2026-11-26 cleanup intentionally removed old temporary QA logs/screenshots. Those historical recipes were not reused as fresh acceptance. The selected original source frames and the current candidate/source/peer facts were freshly checked against retained originals. Compact metadata archives preserve original bytes rather than creating new repeated full diagnostic dumps.\n"
